 "description": "A juvenile Belatz: 2 body regions (B2), a head, 2 eyes, a 2-leaf crest, 2 legs, 2 flaps, a tail; feathers; upright, neck head. Coat: colour lagoon and periwinkle; fluff long and swept; sheen between; feathers between; fur reach bushy tail and ears; second colour butter and ice. Face: head between; beak short; crest between; crown low; eyes between. Shape: waist thick; back line dipping; hind body small; body pear; build stout. Legs & tail: tail curl straight; tail long, thick. Proportions: a large body, a short beak, a low crest, long legs, broad feet, a thick waist, a dipping back, a long tail, wide flaps, a stout build.",
